-- Scene 2: THE SEAM AGREES -- layout width == shaper width --
   layout 164  shaper 163.59  delta 0.40
   layout 19  shaper 18.94  delta 0.06
   layout 63  shaper 63.23  delta 0.23
   layout 59  shaper 58.59  delta 0.40
  [OK] every case agrees within the integer rounding
  [OK] ...and the rounding is the ONLY disagreement

-- Scene 3: it is SHAPING, not counting characters --
   iii = 19 px, WWW = 63 px
  [OK] three narrow letters are narrower than three wide ones
  [OK] ...and neither is the stub's codepoints * size/2 (36)
   arabic joined = 59 px, the same letters apart = 163 px
  [OK] the joined word is measurably narrower than its letters apart

-- Scene 4: THE WIDTH CACHE -- the precondition, measured --
   21 layouts: RmlUi asked 675 times, the shaper ran 26 times
   cache hits: 649
  [OK] RmlUi asks far more than once per string
  [OK] ...but the shaper runs only once per distinct token
  [OK] ...so the cache absorbed the rest
  [OK] shaping did NOT grow with the layouts
  [OK] ...while asking did

